$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-Bromo-N-ethylpentanamide Dimethylformamide (116 μL, 1.50 mmol, 0.1 eq.)
and thionyl chloride (1.63 mL, 22.5 mmol, 1.5 eq.) were added to a
solution of 5-bromovaleric acid (2.71 g, 15.0 mmol, 1.0 eq.) in toluene
(20 mL) and the reaction mixture was stirred at 50 °C for 4 h. The
volatiles were removed under high vacuum, THF (130 mL) was added and the
mixture was cooled to 0 °C. N,N-Diisopropylethylamine (4.2 mL, 24.0 mmol,
1.6 eq.) and ethylamine (2 M solution in THF, 9.0 mL, 18.0 mmol, 1.2 eq.)
were added dropwise. The reaction mixture was stirred for 1 h at 0 °C
before being quenched by the addition of saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution
(100 mL). The reaction mixture was extracted with Et2O (4 × 75 mL) and
the combined organic phases were washed with satured aqueous NaCl
solution (100 mL) before being dried over MgSO4, filtered, and
concentrated in vacuum. The residue was purified by column chromatography
(SiO2, petrol/EtOAc 4:6). The amide as a clear, colourless oil (2.75 g,
13.2 mmol, 88%). Spectral data match those previously reported.11 ν max
(film): 3275 (broad), 2970, 2933, 1640, 1543, 1439, 1276, 1150, 643 cm-1.
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ H = 1.13 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H, CH3), 1.73-1.82
(m, 2H, CH2), 1.84-1.93 (m, 2H, CH2), 2.19 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H, CH2CO),
3.27 (ddt, J = 5.7, 7.4, 14.7 Hz, 2H, NHCH2), 3.41 (t, J = 6.5 Hz, 2H,
BrCH2), 5.79 (br s, 1H, NH). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ C = 14.9 (CH3),
24.3 (CH2), 32.2 (CH2Br), 33.4 (CH2), 34.4 (NHCH2), 35.6 (CH2C=O), 172.2
(C=O). m/z (CI+): 210.0 [M81BrH]+ (80%), 208.0 [M79BrH]+ (80%), 128.1
(100%), 107.1 (60%). HRMS (CI+): calcd for C7H15 81BrNO [M81BrH]+
210.0317, found 210.0320; calcd for C7H15 79BrNO [M79BrH]+ 208.0337,
found 208.0341.
