$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(2-Bromophenyl)-2-hydroxy-N-(4-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenethyl)acetamide
(15) To a solution of 4-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenethylamine hydrochloride
(14) (2.04 g, 10 mmol), 2-bromomandelic acid (9) (2.47 g, 10.5 mmol),
HOBt hydrate (1.68 g, 11 mmol) and N,N-diisopropylethylamine (2 mL, 12
mmol) in anhydrous DMF (10 mL) was added EDC (2.1 g, 11 mmol) under
argon. The resulting mixture was stirred at room temperature for 20 h and
then quenched by the addition of 1 M HCl(aq). The aqueous layer was
extracted with EtOAc (2 × 50 mL). After neutralization with saturated
aqueous NaHCO3, the combined organic extracts were washed with brine,
dried over anhydrous MgSO4, filtered and concentrated. The residue was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc/hexane, 50:50 to
60:40), 15 (3.11 g, 82%) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) 7.50
(1 H, dd, J = 7.5, 1.2 Hz), 7.33 (1 H, dd, J = 8.0, 2.3 Hz), 7.29 (1 H,
td, J = 7.5, 1.2 Hz), 7.17 (1 H, td, J = 8.0, 2.3 Hz), 6.75 (1 H, d, J =
8.0 Hz), 6.60 (1 H, d, J = 2.3 Hz), 6.48 (1 H, dd, J = 8.0, 2.3 Hz), 6.23
(1 H, br, NH), 5.63 (1 H, s, PhOH), 5.41 (1 H, d, J = 4.6 Hz), 4.24 (1 H,
d, J = 4.6 Hz, OH), 3.82 (3 H, s), 3.51-3.49 (2 H, m), 2.74-2.65 (2 H,
m); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) 171.4, 146.5, 144.2, 138.9, 132.8, 129.9 (2
×), 128.5, 128.1, 122.7, 121.2, 114.4, 111.0, 72.0, 55.8, 40.9, 35.0;
HRMS (DART-TOF) m/z calculated for C17H19BrNO4 [M + H]+: 380.0497; found:
380.0485.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthetic Studies of 7-Oxygenated Aporphine Alkaloids: Preparation of
